Verification: run once, from your task checkout's root. Never `cd /mnt/d/projexts/moes`; see mem:decision-doc-row-checkrefs-worktree-mode. Join the two checkRefs with ' && ':

[1] cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" && npm run lint

[2] The doc check, verbatim from /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-8552/checkref-doc.txt (859 chars). It does six things:
- B = merge-base HEAD "${MOE_LAND_TARGET:-HEAD}";
- sec() extracts one `### moe.<tool>` section joined into one line, and strip() drops the three edited sections;
- it fails if any PLANNING/BLOCKED '… cannot go straight to' sentence or 'routed: string[]' remains;
- it needs `routingTargets: string[]` and no `routed` in chat_send;
- it needs 'and from `PLANNING` and `BLOCKED`' in set_task_status, and 'from `PLANNING` or `BLOCKED`', 'workerId?: string' and '`-32003` / `NOT_ALLOWED`' in archive_task;
- it diffs every OTHER section against B, then prints DOC-CHECK-OK.

My dry run: red (exit 1) on today's text, green on the reference edit. A one-character edit in another section turns it red.

Expect the three `OK: docs/roles/…` lint lines, then DOC-CHECK-OK, and exit 0. Submit the joined command, its exit code and the output tail as the complete_task verification. QA in the control checkout: B degrades to HEAD there, so diff `git show <sha>^:docs/MCP_SERVER.md` by hand.
